  "limitations": [
    "The former passenger station and attached train shed are shown circa 1913. The demolition date bounds historical visibility. The full interior, freestanding powerhouse, streetcar track, distant railroad yard and later Magic City sign are outside this scope.",
    "Architect’s drawings, dimensions, early exterior postcards and the 1911 survey govern the model. Decorative relief, actual finish tint, baggage and express wing roof breaks, rails and portions of the rear platform envelope are interpreted.",
    "The present-day original terrain is preserved as an independent reference. Historic floor elevations and the grade of the subway approach are approximate. A narrow modeled road cut reveals the original west portal in geographic views."
  ],
  "sourceLicense": "Original geometry under the repository license. Public-domain Qualla postcards, public-domain 1911 survey, and Marye’s original 1909 U.S. periodical report and drawings. OpenStreetMap tunnel geometry under ODbL 1.0.",
